<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedieos</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pediaios</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pedieos is the longest river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, rising in the Troodos mountains and flowing north-east through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicosia">Nicosia</a> across the Mesaoria plain towards Famagusta Bay. Ancient settlements in its valley included Tamassos, Idalion and Ledra. Like most Cypriot rivers it flows mainly in the wet season.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedieos.jpg" alt="Pedieos" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter in s · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedieos_River.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
